Think: Good, I can see the file_dates.csv contains 4 entries. Now I need to calculate the age in days for each file. Let me use a simpler approach by processing each line individually with awk and the date command.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F',' '{
    cmd = "date -d \"" $2 "\" +%s";
    cmd | getline file_epoch;
    close(cmd);

    cmd2 = "date -d \"2026-01-28\" +%s";
    cmd2 | getline current_epoch;
    close(cmd2);

    age_days = int((current_epoch - file_epoch) / 86400);
    print $1 "," $2 "," age_days;
}' temp_workspace/file_dates.csv > temp_workspace/file_age.csv
```

